{"type":"text","timestamp":1794544882769,"sessionID":"ses_e2ccd2a29ffep4L2jrNUtgPH5n","part":{"id":"prt_1d335c94c001bNKU929AmqkmUW","sessionID":"ses_e2ccd2a29ffep4L2jrNUtgPH5n","messageID":"msg_1d3359e38001i8kdAoS8A543ZW","type":"text","text":"T018 done.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` — in `recommendationFromCli`, immediately after the `ownerSkillId` spread, added the `needsMode` pass-through with its WHY comment.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` — added the `resultFromCliData` case for `{ skillId: 'system-deep-loop', confidence: 0.89, uncertainty: 0.12, needsMode: true }`, asserting the first rendered line contains `use system-deep-loop (needs a mode)`.\n\n**Verify output**\n```\n$ env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD npx vitest run tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  3 passed (3)\nVHFT_exit=0\n\n$ npm run typecheck\n> ../../system-spec-kit/node_modules/.bin/tsc --noEmit --composite false -p tsconfig.build.json\nTC_exit=0\n```\n\n**Deviation to note:** the session exports `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1`, which makes the renderer label a `start` command `(parent-named only)` and breaks the pre-existing `renders a CLI row without command fields` case regardless of this change. `scratch/before.txt` line 2 records that VGT and VHFT are run with `AI_SESSION_CHILD` unset for exactly this reason, so I ran VHFT with `env -u AI_SESSION_CHILD`. The unmodified environment shows 1 failed (that pre-existing case), my new case passes either way.\n\n**Not done:** tasks.md checkbox left unticked as instructed; no git state touched.","time":{"start":1794544879948,"end":1794544882769}}}
